is amping up pressure on Chief Election Commissioner Gyanesh Kumar to resign over alleged voter roll manipulation. DW has more.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trump says taxpayers will no longer fund ads touting administration</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4061805f2f823936b51426b15d96a6178949c1fa536b59cebd34f9b9676360b2</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:37Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T02:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trump-says-taxpayers-will-no-longer-fund-ads-touting-administration/a-79557317--29e1c60009aa.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trump-says-taxpayers-will-no-longer-fund-ads-touting-administration/a-79557317?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Trump faced criticism from across the political divide after at least $1.5 million in federal funds was spent on TV ads. He says his MAGA Inc. super PAC will pay for future ads.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Measles cases are spreading in the US this year, with over 1,000 infections reported in Pennsylvania</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fe9f245590a93bd95df93148c60df80887f4b10d4fe2e224b30cd6855c76376b</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:40Z</updated><published>2026-10-06T01:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/measles-cases-are-spreading-in-the-us-this-year-with-over-1-000-infections-reported-in-pennsylvania/a-79557286--0e8bb1e15eae.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/measles-cases-are-spreading-in-the-us-this-year-with-over-1-000-infections-reported-in-pennsylvania/a-79557286?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A measles outbreak in Pennsylvania has topped 1,000 cases, with neighboring New York declaring a disaster emergency and mobilizing measures to fight the spread.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>ICC unseals Taliban leaders' warrants over persecuting women</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a06152b7bccd5862d371eee8293e1c704ad3cddf4d6052b7676cc3186a61f35a</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:43Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T21:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/icc-unseals-taliban-leaders-warrants-over-persecuting-women/a-79556631--069482e3bddf.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/icc-unseals-taliban-leaders-warrants-over-persecuting-women/a-79556631?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The court gave more details on the warrants for four Taliban leaders accused of the crime against humanity of gender persecution of women, girls and the LGBTQ+ community. The Islamist group rejected the warrants.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australia's migrant policy offers lessons for EU and US</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2c34a0eba4a10d03666339366767e13d3fed0ca422054b8b068ef42e828cbd31</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:47Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T19:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-s-migrant-policy-offers-lessons-for-eu-and-us/a-79388096--ed0adddcf21b.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-s-migrant-policy-offers-lessons-for-eu-and-us/a-79388096?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Australia has used offshore processing centers to deter asylum seekers for more than two decades. As the EU and US pursue similar third-country arrangements, Australia's experience highlights the potential problems.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Yemen launches major military operation against Houthis</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:079b7f22c6f1138ad55dde1e9b787c2a77054411a7d20456dfc5b5f937f38b53</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T18:36:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/yemen-launches-major-military-operation-against-houthis/a-79542723--a2d13f53fcc7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/yemen-launches-major-military-operation-against-houthis/a-79542723?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Yemen's internationally recognized government has launched a new military offensive to retake Houthi-held territory, as the Iran-backed rebel group claims new attacks in Saudi Arabia.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Iran poised to exploit security vacuum as US leaves Iraq</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3c3d7b51b3cad78402c0d22d8db38e0ff4e54b3358f523e8f2d23b3794ed389</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:04:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-poised-to-exploit-security-vacuum-as-us-leaves-iraq/a-79550833--9d1cbb2d4ce5.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-poised-to-exploit-security-vacuum-as-us-leaves-iraq/a-79550833?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The end of the US military mission in Iraq leaves the Kurdistan region facing a severe security vacuum. As Erbil grapples with deep internal divisions, Tehran is well positioned to make strategic gains.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Denmark: Data of millions compromised in hack</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:33d2e3e7cf3cbe3e378a9f518337471fe35245b4ccb6b739e296787d1292f754</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:49Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:46:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/denmark-data-of-millions-compromised-in-hack/a-79555907--9d01221059ac.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/denmark-data-of-millions-compromised-in-hack/a-79555907?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The breach by the hackers was through the legitimate login credentials of a local company, initial findings suggest. The data of some 8.8 million registered people was compromised.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Merz, Macron seek tougher EU measures against unfair trade</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:edd5dfb38662c925f58a0e2da77cb5e910cdbf71ed895338b2735c6b293511de</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:34:52Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T17:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905--9b126d039a17.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/merz-macron-seek-tougher-eu-measures-against-unfair-trade/a-79554905?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Emmanuel Macron and Friedrich Merz have written to Ursula von der Leyen, calling for tougher EU mechanisms against unfair trade practices by other states. They name no names but seem to have China or the US in mind.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Ukraine says Russian drones behind Turkish ship sinking</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:74eb8c07945ccc130241a248537587c281aa277a306eb6211f76eb7042f014c7</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:49:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ukraine-says-russian-drones-behind-turkish-ship-sinking/a-79552387--1f8b019db855.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ukraine-says-russian-drones-behind-turkish-ship-sinking/a-79552387?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Romanian authorities did not say what caused the fire, but local media reported that the ship was carrying grain and was hit by a drone.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Australia, New Zealand probe Flydubai pilot's time there</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:61e837fe5d85919bee93433bef710ef6e6ab95b6f4c6c6b14a5a3f81704433dc</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T15:02:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/australia-new-zealand-probe-flydubai-pilot-s-time-there/a-79551423--4e0d79ffea0c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/australia-new-zealand-probe-flydubai-pilot-s-time-there/a-79551423?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The Flydubai pilot from Oman suspected of trying to crash a plane in Israel spent time in Oceania as a young man. Police in both Australia and New Zealand said they would investigate his links to the countries.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Euro plummets against US dollar: Has the next financial crisis begun?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:8cbd11cc237c1121bb968566f91b0e3162191b2b4090e2f0fd9b6c5c9473bc7a</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031--86ee12acb8f2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/euro-plummets-against-us-dollar-has-the-next-financial-crisis-begun/a-79549031?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The euro has fallen to a 17-month low against the dollar. That will make inflation worse in the EU, where political worries and concern over French debt are already troubling investors. Is a fiscal crisis at hand?</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Military aircraft with 32 people on board crashes in southern Nigeria</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:07b4de91f233cc4bdb9030019085af6454191741f73cd5d7d7d061d898f0adbe</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:05:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/military-aircraft-with-32-people-on-board-crashes-in-southern-nigeria/a-79552403--6ad5344ba083.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/military-aircraft-with-32-people-on-board-crashes-in-southern-nigeria/a-79552403?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Rescue teams searched the crash site after the military aircraft went down in southern Nigeria. All 32 people on the plane are confirmed to have died.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Trust in the German Constitutional Court is eroding — how can this be stopped?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e1953aa5a158114ce031ea7644af2ddcd54085c4ac36fc5a26559d0a7546ab1c</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:03:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211--cc048545c82f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/trust-in-the-german-constitutional-court-is-eroding-how-can-this-be-stopped/a-79549211?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Germany's top court, which turned 75 this year, is losing the population's trust, surveys show. Some say reforms in the way it picks candidates would help, to also accept candidates nominated by the far-right AfD.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>What China's new military foothold in Laos means for Southeast Asia</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cbefa2eb45c3bf8dd31dcd5aec0214fd8727639b00e83447bf6df49d94447cd2</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T14:01:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259--642cd34d5dd0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/what-china-s-new-military-foothold-in-laos-means-for-southeast-asia/a-79548259?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Beijing says its new Laos facility will train pilots. Analysts see a broader signal: China's growing military presence in mainland Southeast Asia.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Germany news: Spy chief warns Russia conflict risk growing</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:f7d371337b55edb51146c147c65a82e30616abba5df5b7a5b4a0fa1318a29806</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T12:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789--3bde17a9e96c.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/germany-news-spy-chief-warns-russia-conflict-risk-growing/live-79542789?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Moscow is already waging a "shadow war" against Europe, the head of Germany's foreign intelligence service says. The Left Party is taking a case over remarks by the CDU's Katherina Reiche to a top court.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Suspected pneumonic plague in Siberia: What we know about the disease</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6717c51eed4063d33da727ef41cc507b39465bac70566b1d94dd92b67e6f06fc</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T11:58:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919--6c7e74a1d6ab.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/suspected-pneumonic-plague-in-siberia-what-we-know-about-the-disease/a-79547919?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A worker at a plague research institute in Siberia has died, and nearly 200 of her contacts are under medical observation. Russian authorities deny a link to the bacterial infection. The US is monitoring the situation.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>German soccer: Can new coach Klopp turn things around?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:17dca57fda324a2d6da764ab07cb78cecd3f996f4468e7418665a74daf04fd4f</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:34:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/german-soccer-can-new-coach-klopp-turn-things-around/a-79547308--04a0262a4a50.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/german-soccer-can-new-coach-klopp-turn-things-around/a-79547308?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Jürgen Klopp has done things a little differently since becoming Germany coach. Casting a wider net for talent and trying to connect with players and country haven't made an immediate impact, but he is not bowed.</summary><category term="Sports" /></entry><entry><title>Bosnia election: New steps to prevent electoral fraud, but nationalist parties remain on top</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0f5a5df80e06a0455860ea481abd60861bdbc40f66a32257cad4787d5f854170</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T10:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717--5102b97990e3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/bosnia-election-new-steps-to-prevent-electoral-fraud-but-nationalist-parties-remain-on-top/a-79544717?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">New technology has stopped votes being cast on behalf of dead or absent voters, and turnout has fallen to a record low. But it was a case of deja vu in Bosnia's elections with the same parties winning.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>As rising seas threaten low-lying Pacific Islands, regional leaders call on the world to take climate more seriously</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:890edafe87d8f690a3e4d3b29c958b49e0884aaddae9d52038f64d5c5dc4a645</id><updated>2026-10-06T06:33:33Z</updated><published>2026-10-05T09:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/as-rising-seas-threaten-low-lying-pacific-islands-regional-leaders-call-on-the-world-to-take-climate/a-79540127--eb759682e424.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/as-rising-seas-threaten-low-lying-pacific-islands-regional-leaders-call-on-the-world-to-take-climate-more-seriously/a-79540127?maca=en-rss-en-top-1022-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For Pacific island nations, climate change is no distant threat. As seas rise, they're bringing the real-time consequences of a warming planet directly to world leaders in Tuvalu.</summary><category term="Climate" /></entry></feed>
